{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"group-perfho","type":"group","x":1880,"y":800,"width":1520,"height":1100,"label":"Perf Hotspots"},
		{"id":"group-perfba","type":"group","x":20,"y":40,"width":540,"height":1780,"label":"Perf Baseline"},
		{"id":"group-perfgu","type":"group","x":640,"y":420,"width":540,"height":640,"label":"Perf Guardrails"},
		{"id":"group-perfre","type":"group","x":1260,"y":420,"width":540,"height":640,"label":"Perf Reporting"},
		{"id":"legend","type":"text","text":"## Legend\n🔴 **Red** = To Do (ready)\n⬜ **Gray** = Blocked\n🟠 **Orange** = Doing\n🔵 **Cyan** = Ready to review\n🟢 **Green** = Done\n🟣 **Purple** = Proposed by agent","x":-540,"y":-310,"width":380,"height":230,"color":"0"},
		{"id":"canvas-warnings","type":"text","text":"## Warnings\n✓ None","x":-540,"y":-530,"width":380,"height":200,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"canvas-errors","type":"text","text":"## Errors\n✓ None","x":-540,"y":-750,"width":380,"height":200,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"3cbdcc10","type":"text","text":"## PB-01 Freeze representative realtime benchmark\nFrozen the conservative benchmark contract in docs/performance_realtime_baseline.md using scripts/profile_simulation.py with 0.2 mm and 0.05 mm meshes, steps=200000, warmup=5000, repeats=2, hotspots=both, and baseline report outputs/profiling/realtime_baseline_20260321.json. Current medians are 37714.66 steps/s at 0.2 mm (26.51x slower than realtime) and 24372.43 steps/s at 0.05 mm (41.03x slower than realtime). Dashboard artifact: outputs/profiling/performance_dashboard.html.","x":80,"y":80,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"d378c8c0","type":"text","text":"## PB-02 Stabilize benchmark conditions\nAdded machine and power-context capture to scripts/profile_simulation.py so each profiling report records host/platform, power source, battery state, active power scheme, processor policy caps, frequency/performance counters, and a comparability assessment. Added the repeatable preset runner scripts/profile_realtime_baseline.py to run the frozen conservative baseline and refresh the HTML dashboard in one command. Updated the dashboard meta panel to surface power context and comparability notes. Verified with pytest tests/test_profile_baseline_preset.py tests/test_perf_dashboard.py -q and a real baseline run to outputs/profiling/realtime_baseline_pb02_verify.json. Fresh baseline medians: 40516.49 steps/s at 0.2 mm and 31411.69 steps/s at 0.05 mm; current run was on AC, Balanced plan, max processor state 100, with no battery or policy-cap warning recorded.","x":80,"y":460,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"c76f8859","type":"text","text":"## PG-01 Define no-regression fidelity checks\nDefined explicit fidelity guardrails in scripts/profile_simulation.py by adding per-scenario fidelity_signature data and optional baseline comparison via --compare-to. Guardrails now cover termination_reason, crater_count, crater_volume_mm3, mean wire temperature, max wire damage, final workpiece position, and dashboard-required signals (wire_temperature, wire_material_positions_mm, wire_head_idx, wire_offset_mm). Regenerated the canonical baseline at outputs/profiling/realtime_baseline_20260322_i1.json so it includes fidelity_signature, updated docs/README with the comparison workflow, and added regression tests in tests/test_profile_fidelity.py. Verified with pytest tests/test_profile_fidelity.py tests/test_profile_baseline_preset.py tests/test_perf_dashboard.py -q (8 passed) and a self-compare of the canonical baseline report.","x":700,"y":460,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"ff634484","type":"text","text":"## PB-03 Reach conservative realtime milestone\nClose the gap to 1,000,000 steps/s on this PC for the conservative benchmark before moving on to more aggressive approximations.","x":80,"y":1600,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"e5f903cc","type":"text","text":"## PB-04 Lower conservative benchmark current to I1\nChange the conservative realtime baseline preset from I5 to I1 so the benchmark avoids wire-broken termination when possible, then regenerate the baseline JSON, docs, and dashboard against the new contract.","x":80,"y":840,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"f34bd19e","type":"text","text":"## PG-02 Automate perf-vs-fidelity verification\nMake it easy to rerun throughput and fidelity checks together before accepting optimizations.","x":700,"y":840,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"803d9f8e","type":"text","text":"## PR-01 Build bottleneck dashboard HTML\nExpanded the performance dashboard in scripts/build_perf_dashboard.py from a static summary into an interactive report. Added a plot control bar with metric selection plus manual y-axis min/max inputs and apply/reset actions, and replaced the flat hotspot section with a module drilldown panel that lets you click a module such as wire and inspect the heaviest matching cProfile functions/lines per scenario. Regenerated outputs/profiling/performance_dashboard.html and tightened tests/test_perf_dashboard.py so the smoke test now covers the new plot controls and drilldown section. Verified with python scripts/build_perf_dashboard.py and pytest tests/test_perf_dashboard.py -q (1 passed).","x":1320,"y":460,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"91bfd94b","type":"text","text":"## PR-02 Track progress history\nExtended the standalone performance dashboard to track archived progress instead of only raw snapshots. scripts/build_perf_dashboard.py now reads verification_summary from candidate reports, computes per-scenario deltas versus the previous archived run and versus the baseline, adds a Before / After panel for the latest verified candidate, and shows Vs previous / Vs baseline columns in both the latest snapshot table and the full history table. Regenerated outputs/profiling/performance_dashboard.html from 10 archived profiling reports, including outputs/profiling/perf_candidate_pg02_pr02_verify.json, and updated README.md plus docs/performance_realtime_baseline.md so the verification-and-history workflow is documented. Verified with pytest tests/test_perf_verification_workflow.py tests/test_perf_dashboard.py tests/test_profile_baseline_preset.py tests/test_profile_fidelity.py -q (10 passed).","x":1320,"y":840,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"21775b2a","type":"text","text":"## PH-03 Reduce environment bookkeeping overhead\nTrim per-step action, observation, reward, and termination overhead after the dominant physics hotspots are under control.","x":1940,"y":1220,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"f9d70be6","type":"text","text":"## PH-02 Reduce ignition short-circuit overhead\nCut the cost of ignition bookkeeping and short-circuit detection while preserving spark statistics and transition behavior.","x":1940,"y":840,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"a1478aa8","type":"text","text":"## PH-05 Eliminate O(N) wire rollover copies","x":1940,"y":1600,"width":420,"height":260,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"e2af75aa","type":"text","text":"## PH-06 Reduce wire state-sync and export copy cost\nTrim the per-step sync/export overhead in the wire path without weakening the logging contract. Target wire_temperature, wire_damage, wire_material_positions_mm, head/offset diagnostics, and any fallback copies that still happen every step.","x":2430,"y":1600,"width":420,"height":260,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"2aa0fa92","type":"text","text":"## PH-07 Reduce wire thermal-core memory traffic\nOptimize the thermal part of WireModule.update after PH-04 exposes its share. Focus on fused or in-place conduction, Joule-heating, plasma, and convection updates so the wire core stops creating avoidable full-array temporaries at fine meshes.","x":2920,"y":1600,"width":420,"height":260,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"2fd8a300","type":"text","text":"## PH-04 Instrument wire sub-buckets\nBreak WireModule.update into measured sub-buckets in the profiling harness and dashboard: transport/rollover, thermal core, damage, and state sync/export. The current wire hotspot is too monolithic; this task creates the internal breakdown needed to choose the next optimization with data instead of guesswork.","x":2430,"y":1220,"width":420,"height":180,"color":"4"}
	],
